# Protocol: Spoken [Language] — [Variety]

> **SETUP AGENT: this is a synthesis template.** Write the live file to
> `protocol/dialect.md`; delete every guidance blockquote. This is the most-edited pack file
> after setup: the learner's native resources will correct it, and every correction lands
> here. Every rule carries a written-vs-spoken example in the target language. Worked
> example: `docs/WORKED_EXAMPLE.md` → Dialect (a strongly diglossic language; yours may be
> close to its written form, and then this file is short).

> **Read by every pass that can emit target language a voice will speak** — through
> `writer.voice_canon()`, the single owner — and by the studio Producer. A lane that writes
> speech without this file writes the textbook register, and native listeners hear it at
> once.

The test for every line: *would someone from [place] say this to a friend?* If it sounds
like a textbook or a news anchor, it needs work.

